description:
In `mergeItems` (lane.ts lines 109-119):
- `labels` are appended in gel-position order;
- `sizes` are then re-sorted largest first;
- fragments without a label add nothing to `labels`.

When forms are mixed, or when some fragments are unlabelled, `labels[i]` does not describe `sizes[i]`. A UI that explains a merged band (tooltip: "which fragment is which?") pairs labels with the wrong sizes, and cannot map the band back to its input fragments.

The failing regression tests in lane.test.ts ("review: a merged band can be traced back to its fragments") already cover this defect.

